From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20M=C3=A9ndez=20Rey?= <vejeta@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:49:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Fix crashes on missing users and long command-line
 arguments

- Several checks dereferenced getpwnam()/getpwuid() results directly, so
  conquer and conqrun crashed (segmentation fault) when LOGIN or the god
  nation's leader is not a user on this system, e.g. a world or a binary
  built on another machine, or a container. Add login_uid() and
  uid_name(), which return -1 and "(unknown)" for unknown users, and use
  them everywhere the result was not checked.
- conqrun -d copied its argument into an 80-byte buffer without a length
  check (a buffer overflow with long paths, caught by glibc's fortify
  check and AddressSanitizer), and conquer -n copied the nation name
  into a 10-byte buffer. Reject names that are too long with a message,
  bound the data= copy from CONQ_OPTS, always terminate the copied
  environment string and use snprintf for the data directory paths.

Checked with AddressSanitizer and UBSan: long -d and -n arguments now
fail cleanly and a full turn update reports no errors; with a LOGIN user
that does not exist, conqrun -x refuses to run instead of crashing.
